            <div xml:id="d1218">

                <pb facs="1266" n="1254" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/8–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-19T16:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1017. ReEmb 385, March 21, 1945. Turkish-Soviet Treaty of December 17, 1925 and
                    its protocols will expire November 7, 1945. Estimate of probable effect of
                    expiration on Turkish-Soviet relations would be useful.</p>
                <p>Sent to Ankara as Department’s 1017, repeated to Moscow as Department’s 2188, and
                    to London as Department’s 9254.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
